class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(String s) {
        int l = 0, r = s.length() - 1;
        while (l < r) {
            while (l < r && !Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(l))) l++;
            while (l < r && !Character.isLetterOrDigit(s.charAt(r))) r--;
            if (Character.toLowerCase(s.charAt(l)) != Character.toLowerCase(s.charAt(r))) {
                return false;
            }
            l++;
            r--;
        }
        return true;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int[] twoSum(int[] numbers, int target) {
        int l = 0, r = numbers.length - 1;
        while (l < r) {
            int sum = numbers[l] + numbers[r];
            if (sum == target) return new int[]{l + 1, r + 1};
            if (sum < target) l++;
            else r--;
        }
        return new int[0];
    }
}

class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> threeSum(int[] nums) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length - 2; i++) {
            if (nums[i] > 0) break;
            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;
            int l = i + 1, r = nums.length - 1;
            while (l < r) {
                int sum = nums[i] + nums[l] + nums[r];
                if (sum == 0) {
                    res.add(Arrays.asList(nums[i], nums[l], nums[r]));
                    l++;
                    r--;
                    while (l < r && nums[l] == nums[l - 1]) l++;
                    while (l < r && nums[r] == nums[r + 1]) r--;
                } else if (sum < 0) {
                    l++;
                } else {
                    r--;
                }
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> fourSum(int[] nums, int target) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int n = nums.length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 3; i++) {
            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n - 2; j++) {
                if (j > i + 1 && nums[j] == nums[j - 1]) continue;
                int l = j + 1, r = n - 1;
                while (l < r) {
                    long sum = (long) nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[l] + nums[r];
                    if (sum == target) {
                        res.add(Arrays.asList(nums[i], nums[j], nums[l], nums[r]));
                        l++;
                        r--;
                        while (l < r && nums[l] == nums[l - 1]) l++;
                        while (l < r && nums[r] == nums[r + 1]) r--;
                    } else if (sum < target) {
                        l++;
                    } else {
                        r--;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int maxArea(int[] height) {
        int l = 0, r = height.length - 1, best = 0;
        while (l < r) {
            int area = Math.min(height[l], height[r]) * (r - l);
            best = Math.max(best, area);
            if (height[l] < height[r]) l++;
            else r--;
        }
        return best;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int trap(int[] height) {
        int l = 0, r = height.length - 1;
        int leftMax = 0, rightMax = 0, water = 0;
        while (l < r) {
            if (height[l] < height[r]) {
                leftMax = Math.max(leftMax, height[l]);
                water += leftMax - height[l];
                l++;
            } else {
                rightMax = Math.max(rightMax, height[r]);
                water += rightMax - height[r];
                r--;
            }
        }
        return water;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int removeDuplicates(int[] nums) {
        int write = 1;
        for (int read = 1; read < nums.length; read++) {
            if (nums[read] != nums[write - 1]) {
                nums[write++] = nums[read];
            }
        }
        return write;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public void moveZeroes(int[] nums) {
        int write = 0;
        for (int read = 0; read < nums.length; read++) {
            if (nums[read] != 0) {
                int t = nums[write];
                nums[write] = nums[read];
                nums[read] = t;
                write++;
            }
        }
    }
}

patterns.intro:
**Sliding Window** maintains a contiguous range `[left, right]` over an array or string and slides it forward, updating a running state (sum, counts, distinct chars) in O(1) per step instead of recomputing each subarray.

**How to recognize it**
- "Longest / shortest / count of **contiguous** subarray or substring such that ..."
- The constraint is **monotonic**: if a window is invalid, growing it keeps it invalid (or shrinking keeps it valid). Typically: all positive numbers, "at most K distinct", "at most K replacements", "contains all chars of T".
- Fixed size `k` windows (max of each window, anagram of length k).

**Variable-size template (longest valid window)**
```java
int left = 0, best = 0;
int[] count = new int[128];          // window state
for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
    count[s.charAt(right)]++;        // 1. expand: add s[right]
    while (windowInvalid()) {        // 2. shrink until valid again
        count[s.charAt(left)]--;
        left++;
    }
    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1); // 3. record answer
}
```
For **shortest** valid window, record the answer *inside* the while loop (while it is still valid) and then shrink.

**Fixed-size template**
```java
for (int right = 0; right < n; right++) {
    add(nums[right]);
    if (right >= k) remove(nums[right - k]);
    if (right >= k - 1) record();
}
```

**Pitfalls**
- Sliding window fails with **negative numbers** for sum targets - use prefix sums + HashMap.
- Off-by-one: window length is `right - left + 1`.
- For "exactly K" problems use `atMost(K) - atMost(K - 1)`.
- Each element enters and leaves the window once, so total time is O(n) even with the inner `while`.

problems.solution:
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {
        int[] last = new int[128];
        Arrays.fill(last, -1);
        int left = 0, best = 0;
        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
            char c = s.charAt(right);
            if (last[c] >= left) left = last[c] + 1;
            last[c] = right;
            best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
        }
        return best;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int characterReplacement(String s, int k) {
        int[] count = new int[26];
        int left = 0, maxFreq = 0, best = 0;
        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
            maxFreq = Math.max(maxFreq, ++count[s.charAt(right) - 'A']);
            while (right - left + 1 - maxFreq > k) {
                count[s.charAt(left) - 'A']--;
                left++;
            }
            best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
        }
        return best;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public boolean checkInclusion(String s1, String s2) {
        int k = s1.length();
        if (k > s2.length()) return false;
        int[] need = new int[26], window = new int[26];
        for (char c : s1.toCharArray()) need[c - 'a']++;
        for (int right = 0; right < s2.length(); right++) {
            window[s2.charAt(right) - 'a']++;
            if (right >= k) window[s2.charAt(right - k) - 'a']--;
            if (right >= k - 1 && Arrays.equals(need, window)) return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public String minWindow(String s, String t) {
        int[] need = new int[128];
        for (char c : t.toCharArray()) need[c]++;
        int missing = t.length();
        int left = 0, bestStart = 0, bestLen = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
            char c = s.charAt(right);
            if (need[c] > 0) missing--;
            need[c]--;
            while (missing == 0) {
                if (right - left + 1 < bestLen) {
                    bestLen = right - left + 1;
                    bestStart = left;
                }
                char d = s.charAt(left++);
                need[d]++;
                if (need[d] > 0) missing++;
            }
        }
        return bestLen == Integer.MAX_VALUE ? "" : s.substring(bestStart, bestStart + bestLen);
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int[] maxSlidingWindow(int[] nums, int k) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int[] res = new int[n - k + 1];
        Deque<Integer> dq = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (!dq.isEmpty() && dq.peekFirst() <= i - k) dq.pollFirst();
            while (!dq.isEmpty() && nums[dq.peekLast()] <= nums[i]) dq.pollLast();
            dq.offerLast(i);
            if (i >= k - 1) res[i - k + 1] = nums[dq.peekFirst()];
        }
        return res;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int longestOnes(int[] nums, int k) {
        int left = 0, zeros = 0, best = 0;
        for (int right = 0; right < nums.length; right++) {
            if (nums[right] == 0) zeros++;
            while (zeros > k) {
                if (nums[left] == 0) zeros--;
                left++;
            }
            best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
        }
        return best;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int totalFruit(int[] fruits) {
        Map<Integer, Integer> count = new HashMap<>();
        int left = 0, best = 0;
        for (int right = 0; right < fruits.length; right++) {
            count.merge(fruits[right], 1, Integer::sum);
            while (count.size() > 2) {
                int f = fruits[left++];
                if (count.merge(f, -1, Integer::sum) == 0) count.remove(f);
            }
            best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);
        }
        return best;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int minSubArrayLen(int target, int[] nums) {
        int left = 0, sum = 0, best = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        for (int right = 0; right < nums.length; right++) {
            sum += nums[right];
            while (sum >= target) {
                best = Math.min(best, right - left + 1);
                sum -= nums[left++];
            }
        }
        return best == Integer.MAX_VALUE ? 0 : best;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public boolean isValid(String s) {
        Deque<Character> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '(') st.push(')');
            else if (c == '[') st.push(']');
            else if (c == '{') st.push('}');
            else if (st.isEmpty() || st.pop() != c) return false;
        }
        return st.isEmpty();
    }
}

class MinStack {
    private final Deque<int[]> st = new ArrayDeque<>(); // {value, minSoFar}

    public MinStack() { }

    public void push(int val) {
        int min = st.isEmpty() ? val : Math.min(val, st.peek()[1]);
        st.push(new int[]{val, min});
    }

    public void pop() {
        st.pop();
    }

    public int top() {
        return st.peek()[0];
    }

    public int getMin() {
        return st.peek()[1];
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int evalRPN(String[] tokens) {
        Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (String t : tokens) {
            switch (t) {
                case "+" -> st.push(st.pop() + st.pop());
                case "*" -> st.push(st.pop() * st.pop());
                case "-" -> { int b = st.pop(), a = st.pop(); st.push(a - b); }
                case "/" -> { int b = st.pop(), a = st.pop(); st.push(a / b); }
                default -> st.push(Integer.parseInt(t));
            }
        }
        return st.pop();
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int[] dailyTemperatures(int[] temperatures) {
        int n = temperatures.length;
        int[] ans = new int[n];
        Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            while (!st.isEmpty() && temperatures[st.peek()] < temperatures[i]) {
                int j = st.pop();
                ans[j] = i - j;
            }
            st.push(i);
        }
        return ans;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int[] nextGreaterElement(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {
        Map<Integer, Integer> next = new HashMap<>();
        Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (int x : nums2) {
            while (!st.isEmpty() && st.peek() < x) next.put(st.pop(), x);
            st.push(x);
        }
        int[] res = new int[nums1.length];
        for (int i = 0; i < nums1.length; i++) {
            res[i] = next.getOrDefault(nums1[i], -1);
        }
        return res;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int largestRectangleArea(int[] heights) {
        int n = heights.length, best = 0;
        Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
            int h = (i == n) ? 0 : heights[i];
            while (!st.isEmpty() && heights[st.peek()] >= h) {
                int height = heights[st.pop()];
                int leftBoundary = st.isEmpty() ? -1 : st.peek();
                best = Math.max(best, height * (i - leftBoundary - 1));
            }
            st.push(i);
        }
        return best;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int carFleet(int target, int[] position, int[] speed) {
        int n = position.length;
        Integer[] idx = new Integer[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) idx[i] = i;
        Arrays.sort(idx, (a, b) -> position[b] - position[a]); // closest to target first
        int fleets = 0;
        double slowest = 0;
        for (int i : idx) {
            double time = (double) (target - position[i]) / speed[i];
            if (time > slowest) {
                fleets++;
                slowest = time;
            }
        }
        return fleets;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int[] asteroidCollision(int[] asteroids) {
        Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
        for (int a : asteroids) {
            boolean alive = true;
            while (alive && a < 0 && !st.isEmpty() && st.peek() > 0) {
                if (st.peek() < -a) {
                    st.pop();
                } else if (st.peek() == -a) {
                    st.pop();
                    alive = false;
                } else {
                    alive = false;
                }
            }
            if (alive) st.push(a);
        }
        int[] res = new int[st.size()];
        for (int i = res.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) res[i] = st.pop();
        return res;
    }
}

class StockSpanner {
    private final Deque<int[]> st = new ArrayDeque<>(); // {price, span}

    public StockSpanner() { }

    public int next(int price) {
        int span = 1;
        while (!st.isEmpty() && st.peek()[0] <= price) {
            span += st.pop()[1];
        }
        st.push(new int[]{price, span});
        return span;
    }
}

patterns.intro:
**Binary Search** repeatedly halves a search space whose elements satisfy a **monotonic** condition: everything on one side is "false", everything on the other is "true". It turns O(n) into O(log n).

**Two kinds of questions**
1. **Search in a sorted (or rotated / 2D) array** - find a target, first/last occurrence, insertion point, peak.
2. **Binary search on the answer** - the answer is a number in a range `[lo, hi]`, and there is a `feasible(x)` check that is monotonic ("if speed x works, any faster speed works too"). Examples: Koko eating bananas, ship packages in D days, split array largest sum, aggressive cows, allocate books.

**How to recognize "search on answer":** the question says *minimize the maximum* / *maximize the minimum* / *smallest X such that...*, and checking a candidate is easy (greedy O(n)).

**Template - first index where condition is true (lower bound)**
```java
int lo = 0, hi = n;              // hi = n means "not found"
while (lo < hi) {
    int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2; // avoids overflow
    if (condition(mid)) hi = mid; // mid might be the answer, keep it
    else lo = mid + 1;            // mid is definitely not it
}
return lo;
```

**Template - minimum feasible answer**
```java
int lo = minPossible, hi = maxPossible;
while (lo < hi) {
    int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
    if (feasible(mid)) hi = mid;
    else lo = mid + 1;
}
return lo;
```

**Pitfalls**
- `(lo + hi) / 2` can overflow - use `lo + (hi - lo) / 2`.
- Infinite loops: with `lo < hi` and `lo = mid`, use an upper mid `lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2`.
- Mixing styles: `while (lo <= hi)` pairs with `hi = mid - 1`; `while (lo < hi)` pairs with `hi = mid`. Pick one style and stick to it.
- Feasibility sums can overflow `int` - use `long`.

problems.solution:
class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int lo = 0, hi = nums.length - 1;
        while (lo <= hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (nums[mid] == target) return mid;
            if (nums[mid] < target) lo = mid + 1;
            else hi = mid - 1;
        }
        return -1;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public boolean searchMatrix(int[][] matrix, int target) {
        int m = matrix.length, n = matrix[0].length;
        int lo = 0, hi = m * n - 1;
        while (lo <= hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            int val = matrix[mid / n][mid % n];
            if (val == target) return true;
            if (val < target) lo = mid + 1;
            else hi = mid - 1;
        }
        return false;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int search(int[] nums, int target) {
        int lo = 0, hi = nums.length - 1;
        while (lo <= hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (nums[mid] == target) return mid;
            if (nums[lo] <= nums[mid]) {                 // left half sorted
                if (nums[lo] <= target && target < nums[mid]) hi = mid - 1;
                else lo = mid + 1;
            } else {                                     // right half sorted
                if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[hi]) lo = mid + 1;
                else hi = mid - 1;
            }
        }
        return -1;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int findMin(int[] nums) {
        int lo = 0, hi = nums.length - 1;
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (nums[mid] > nums[hi]) lo = mid + 1;
            else hi = mid;
        }
        return nums[lo];
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int[] searchRange(int[] nums, int target) {
        int first = lowerBound(nums, target);
        if (first == nums.length || nums[first] != target) return new int[]{-1, -1};
        int last = lowerBound(nums, target + 1) - 1;
        return new int[]{first, last};
    }

    private int lowerBound(int[] nums, int x) {
        int lo = 0, hi = nums.length;
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (nums[mid] >= x) hi = mid;
            else lo = mid + 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int minEatingSpeed(int[] piles, int h) {
        int lo = 1, hi = 0;
        for (int p : piles) hi = Math.max(hi, p);
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (hours(piles, mid) <= h) hi = mid;
            else lo = mid + 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }

    private long hours(int[] piles, int k) {
        long total = 0;
        for (int p : piles) total += (p + k - 1) / k;
        return total;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int shipWithinDays(int[] weights, int days) {
        int lo = 0, hi = 0;
        for (int w : weights) {
            lo = Math.max(lo, w);
            hi += w;
        }
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (daysNeeded(weights, mid) <= days) hi = mid;
            else lo = mid + 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }

    private int daysNeeded(int[] weights, int cap) {
        int days = 1, load = 0;
        for (int w : weights) {
            if (load + w > cap) {
                days++;
                load = 0;
            }
            load += w;
        }
        return days;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int splitArray(int[] nums, int k) {
        int lo = 0, hi = 0;
        for (int x : nums) {
            lo = Math.max(lo, x);
            hi += x;
        }
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (pieces(nums, mid) <= k) hi = mid;
            else lo = mid + 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }

    private int pieces(int[] nums, int limit) {
        int count = 1, sum = 0;
        for (int x : nums) {
            if (sum + x > limit) {
                count++;
                sum = 0;
            }
            sum += x;
        }
        return count;
    }
}

class Solution {
    public int findPeakElement(int[] nums) {
        int lo = 0, hi = nums.length - 1;
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (nums[mid] < nums[mid + 1]) lo = mid + 1;
            else hi = mid;
        }
        return lo;
    }
}

class TimeMap {
    private final Map<String, List<Integer>> times = new HashMap<>();
    private final Map<String, List<String>> values = new HashMap<>();

    public TimeMap() { }

    public void set(String key, String value, int timestamp) {
        times.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(timestamp);
        values.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(value);
    }

    public String get(String key, int timestamp) {
        List<Integer> ts = times.get(key);
        if (ts == null) return "";
        int lo = 0, hi = ts.size();          // first index with time > timestamp
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
            if (ts.get(mid) > timestamp) hi = mid;
            else lo = mid + 1;
        }
        return lo == 0 ? "" : values.get(key).get(lo - 1);
    }
}

class Solution {
    public double findMedianSortedArrays(int[] a, int[] b) {
        if (a.length > b.length) return findMedianSortedArrays(b, a);
        int m = a.length, n = b.length, half = (m + n + 1) / 2;
        int lo = 0, hi = m;
        while (lo <= hi) {
            int i = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;   // taken from a
            int j = half - i;             // taken from b
            int aLeft = i == 0 ? Integer.MIN_VALUE : a[i - 1];
            int aRight = i == m ? Integer.MAX_VALUE : a[i];
            int bLeft = j == 0 ? Integer.MIN_VALUE : b[j - 1];
            int bRight = j == n ? Integer.MAX_VALUE : b[j];
            if (aLeft <= bRight && bLeft <= aRight) {
                int leftMax = Math.max(aLeft, bLeft);
                if (((m + n) & 1) == 1) return leftMax;
                return (leftMax + (double) Math.min(aRight, bRight)) / 2.0;
            } else if (aLeft > bRight) {
                hi = i - 1;
            } else {
                lo = i + 1;
            }
        }
        return 0.0;
    }
}

patterns.intro:
**Linked List** problems test pointer manipulation without losing references. Almost every question is built from a few primitives: **dummy head**, **reverse**, **fast/slow pointers**, and **merge**.

**How to recognize the technique**
- Head might change (delete/insert at front, merging) -> use a **dummy node** pointing at head; return `dummy.next`.
- Middle of list, cycle detection, "nth from end" -> **fast & slow pointers**.
- Palindrome check, reorder, k-group -> **reverse** part of the list.
- Sorted lists combined -> **merge** (two pointers or a heap for k lists).
- O(1) get/put with order (LRU) -> **HashMap + doubly linked list**.

LeetCode's node: `class ListNode { int val; ListNode next; ListNode(int val) {...} ListNode(int val, ListNode next) {...} }` (already defined in the judge).

**Core templates**
```java
// Reverse a list iteratively
ListNode prev = null, cur = head;
while (cur != null) {
    ListNode next = cur.next;
    cur.next = prev;
    prev = cur;
    cur = next;
}
// prev is the new head

// Find middle (slow ends at the 2nd middle for even length)
ListNode slow = head, fast = head;
while (fast != null && fast.next != null) {
    slow = slow.next;
    fast = fast.next.next;
}

// Dummy head for building a result
ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0), tail = dummy;
// ... tail.next = node; tail = tail.next;
return dummy.next;
```

**Pitfalls**
- Save `cur.next` **before** you overwrite it.
- Check `fast != null && fast.next != null` in that order to avoid NPEs.
- Draw the pointers for a 3-node list on paper before coding - interviewers expect you to walk through an example.
- Remember to terminate lists (set `tail.next = null`) when splitting, or you'll create cycles.

